from pathlib import Path
import json,re,html,argparse
parser=argparse.ArgumentParser();parser.add_argument('--source',type=Path,required=True);args=parser.parse_args()
root=args.source.resolve()
p=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]/'games/quintarc/index.html'
s=p.read_text();elements=['Fire','Water','Earth','Air','Arcane'];profiles=json.loads((root/'data/enemy_resistances.json').read_text())
names={'wraith':'Bonebound','skitter':'Dusk Bat','spitter':'Blight Slime','brute':'Ossuary Warden','sentinel':'Crypt Sentinel','thorn':'Hollow Seer','eraser':'Ash Drake'}
rows=[]
for key,r in profiles.items():
 status=', '.join(('immune to '+k.title() if v==0 else f'{k.title()} duration −{(1-v)*100:g}%') for k,v in r['statuses'].items()) or 'No special status resistance'
 rows.append(f'<tr><th scope="row">{names[key]}</th><td>{elements[r["element"]]} −{r["resistance"]*100:g}%</td><td>{elements[r["weakness"]]+" +"+str(round(r["bonus"]*100))+"%" if r["weakness"]>=0 else "None"}</td><td>{(1-r["control"])*100:g}% shorter</td><td>{r["displacement"]*100:g}% distance</td><td>{status}</td></tr>')
block='''<section class="wiki-section" id="elemental-counters"><h2>Elemental counters &amp; resistance</h2><p>The arena matters: <strong>Fire ↔ Water</strong> and <strong>Earth ↔ Air</strong> counter each other. Arcane has no opposing element. Matching orbs strengthen your spell; orbs opposed by the arena weaken it. The effect is weighted by the five orbs in the recipe.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Arena</th><th>Matching element</th><th>Countered element</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Ember Caldera</td><td>Fire</td><td>Water</td></tr><tr><td>Tidal Sanctuary</td><td>Water</td><td>Fire</td></tr><tr><td>Verdant Ruins</td><td>Earth</td><td>Air</td></tr><tr><td>Zephyr Isles</td><td>Air</td><td>Earth</td></tr><tr><td>Astral Paradox</td><td>Arcane</td><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Five matching orbs give <strong>+25% potency</strong>; five countered orbs give <strong>−20%</strong>. For example, 3 Fire + 2 Water in a Fire arena gives +15% −8% = <strong>+7%</strong>. Other elements are neutral. Damage, recovery, shield strength and numerical buff bonuses scale with potency. Spell range, movement distance and ordinary status duration do not scale with map affinity.</p><h3>Know your opponent</h3><p>Enemy resistance is separate from the arena and scales by the elements in the spell. A pure Earth attack deals 35% less damage to an Ossuary Warden; a pure Air attack deals 20% more. Mixed recipes apply only the corresponding fraction of each modifier. Arena potency and enemy resistance multiply.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Enemy</th><th>Resists damage</th><th>Weakness</th><th>Control duration</th><th>Push / pull / throw</th><th>Special status resistance</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+''.join(rows)+'''</tbody></table></div><p>Control resistance affects Stun, Freeze, Root, Silence and Slow. It also reduces Slow’s movement penalty. Special status modifiers multiply with control resistance when both apply. Poison, Burn, Freeze and Shock damage ticks also respect elemental damage resistance.</p><p>Sturdy enemies with control resistance develop temporary resistance to repeated <strong>Stun, Freeze and Root</strong>: each successful application halves the next duration, down to one eighth of the already-resistant duration. Four seconds without another application resets this. A refresh cannot shorten a stronger control effect that is already active.</p><h3>Campaign bosses</h3><p>Campaign bosses resist their chapter’s element by <strong>35%</strong> (the Fire boss: <strong>45%</strong>) and take <strong>20% more</strong> from its opposing element. The Arcane boss has no elemental weakness. Boss control durations are 65% shorter, and push/pull/throw distance is 20% of normal. Their creature’s special status resistance remains: the dragon cannot Burn, and Freeze duration is further halved. Resistance does not make every boss immune to control.</p></section><section class="wiki-section" id="spell-counterplay"><h2>Waves, shields &amp; counterplay</h2><p>Friendly waves pass through one another. Opposing wave fronts clash: strengths within 10% cancel both waves; otherwise the stronger wave continues with the weaker wave’s damage subtracted and proportionally less knockback. This rule applies to wave skills, not every pair of spell effects. Waves push eligible enemies, with walls and resistance limiting displacement.</p><p><strong>Terra Nexus</strong> creates a visible dome with 180 base health, a 6m radius and a 5-second lifetime. It blocks magic crossing the boundary <strong>in either direction, for either team</strong>. Allies shelter inside, but cannot fire through it. Enemies who enter are protected from outside spells too. Players may walk through; spells cast and resolved entirely inside still work. Attacks can break the dome, including allied attacks.</p><p>Personal shields protect only their wearer from all directions and use a close-fitting shell. Construct walls cover the directions their geometry actually blocks; opponents can attack around their sides or behind them. Steam Quake now erupts at the caster’s feet and strikes moving enemies nearby.</p><p>Active buffs and debuffs appear at the bottom left as circular icons with remaining seconds and draining timer rings. Choose your character and available cosmetic accessories in <strong>Your Sage</strong>.</p></section>'''
for id in ['elemental-counters','spell-counterplay']:
 s=re.sub(r'<section class="wiki-section" id="'+id+r'">.*?</section>','',s,flags=re.S)
s=s.replace('<section class="wiki-section" id="spells">',block+'<section class="wiki-section" id="spells">') if 'id="spells"' in s else s
assert 'id="elemental-counters"' in s
nav='<a href="#elemental-counters">Elemental counters &amp; resistance</a><a href="#spell-counterplay">Waves &amp; shields</a>'
s=re.sub(r'<a href="#(?:elemental-counters|spell-counterplay)">.*?</a>','',s)
s=s.replace('<a href="#spells">',nav+'<a href="#spells">',1)
p.write_text(s)
css=p.parents[2]/'style.css'
c=css.read_text()
if '.table-scroll{' not in c:c+='\n.table-scroll{max-width:100%;overflow-x:auto;margin-block:20px}.table-scroll table{min-width:580px;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}.table-scroll th,.table-scroll td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}\n'
css.write_text(c)
